## Component Structure
- Use Livewire components for interactive elements that require server communication
- Keep Livewire components focused on a single responsibility
- Break down complex UI into smaller, reusable Livewire components
- Use proper naming conventions for component properties and methods
- Leverage component inheritance for shared functionality
- Structure your component directories by feature rather than component type

## Data Handling
- Utilize Livewire's built-in validation system
- Use computed properties for derived data instead of storing redundant state
- Apply property type hints to ensure data integrity
- Use properly scoped data binding with wire:model.defer when appropriate
- Implement proper error handling in Livewire components
- Be mindful of property visibility (public vs protected vs private)

## Performance
- Optimize Livewire components for performance by minimizing DOM changes
- Use debounce and throttle modifiers to reduce unnecessary server calls
- Implement lazy loading for components not visible on initial page load
- Keep the payload size small by only including necessary properties
- Use polling judiciously to avoid unnecessary server load
- Implement proper caching strategies for expensive operations

## Lifecycle Management
- Use Livewire's lifecycle hooks effectively (mount, hydrate, updated, etc.)
- Understand the component lifecycle to optimize loading and rendering
- Clean up resources in the dehydrate method when appropriate
- Use the right lifecycle method for data loading to avoid duplicate queries
- Implement proper state initialization in the mount method
- Use the updating/updated hooks to respond to property changes

## Integration
- Properly integrate with Alpine.js for client-side interactions
- Use events for communication between components
- Implement proper JavaScript interoperability when needed
- Follow Laravel's conventions for routing and responses
- Use Livewire alongside traditional Laravel controllers where appropriate
- Leverage third-party packages like Livewire PowerGrid for complex data tables
